WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.541
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:11.221
Dad?

00:00:11.256 --> 00:00:13.316
Sam. This is bigger than you
think. They're everywhere.

00:00:13.351 --> 00:00:15.404
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:15.439 --> 00:00:17.668
Saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:17.703 --> 00:00:19.175
The family business.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:20.648
I got to find dad.

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:23.578
I dreamt about Jessica's
death before it happened.

00:00:23.613 --> 00:00:24.543
You got to be careful, all right?

00:00:24.578 --> 00:00:27.164
Ghosts are attracted to that
whole ESP thing you got going.

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:29.580
I told you I don't have ESP.
I just have strange vibes.

00:00:29.615 --> 00:00:32.801
Weird dreams. Dead people
have weird dreams, man.

00:00:32.836 --> 00:00:35.987
I have these nightmares.
Sometimes they come true.

00:00:36.291 --> 00:00:37.587
Come again?

00:02:06.346 --> 00:02:08.736
Somebody help me! Somebody...!

00:02:09.383 --> 00:02:11.177
Somebody help...!

00:02:41.666 --> 00:02:42.683
Dean.

00:02:43.942 --> 00:02:45.211
Dean.

00:02:47.877 --> 00:02:50.438
What are you doing, man? It's
in the middle of the night.

00:02:50.656 --> 00:02:52.428
We have to go.

00:02:52.603 --> 00:02:54.685
What's happening? We have to go.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.218
Right now.

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:01.795
Mcreedy.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.205
Detective Mcreedy. Badge number 158.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.621
I've got a signal four
eighty on progress.

00:03:06.656 --> 00:03:10.124
I need a registered
owner of a Two door Sedan.

00:03:10.159 --> 00:03:13.592
Michigan license plate
Mary, Frank, 6-0-3-7.

00:03:13.627 --> 00:03:15.069
Yeah, okay. Just hurry.

00:03:15.104 --> 00:03:16.473
Sammy, relax.

00:03:16.508 --> 00:03:19.758
I'm sure, its just a nightmare.
Yeah. Tell me about it.

00:03:19.793 --> 00:03:23.008
I mean it. You know, a normal
everyday naked class nightmare.

00:03:23.043 --> 00:03:25.359
This license plate, it
won't check out. You'll see.

00:03:25.394 --> 00:03:27.270
It felt different Dean. Real.

00:03:27.305 --> 00:03:29.726
Like we dreamt about our
old house and Jessica.

00:03:29.761 --> 00:03:32.612
Oh, yeah. That makes sense. Dreaming
about our house, your girlfriend.

00:03:32.647 --> 00:03:34.471
This guy in your dream,
you ever seen him before?

00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:36.003
No... No, exactly.

00:03:36.038 --> 00:03:38.687
Why would you have premonitions
about some random dude in Michigan?

00:03:38.722 --> 00:03:40.044
I don't know. Yeah, me neither.

00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:41.475
Yes, I'm here.

00:03:45.143 --> 00:03:47.718
Jim Miller, Saginaw Michigan.

00:03:47.753 --> 00:03:50.294
You have the street address?

00:03:51.095 --> 00:03:53.450
Got it. Thanks.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.139
It checks out.

00:03:57.174 --> 00:03:58.768
How far are we?

00:03:59.759 --> 00:04:01.086
From Saginaw? Yeah.

00:04:01.121 --> 00:04:02.799
A couple of hours.

00:04:04.507 --> 00:04:06.403
Drive faster.

00:04:57.171 --> 00:04:58.659
What happened?

00:04:58.694 --> 00:05:00.645
Suicide.

00:05:01.309 --> 00:05:04.022
I can't believe it.

00:05:05.977 --> 00:05:07.591
Did you know him?

00:05:07.626 --> 00:05:11.390
Saw him everyday at Saint Augustine.

00:05:11.425 --> 00:05:15.155
Always seems... seemed so normal.

00:05:15.331 --> 00:05:18.413
I guess you never know what's
going behind closed doors.

00:05:18.448 --> 00:05:21.107
I guess not. How did uh...

00:05:21.142 --> 00:05:23.732
What are they saying happened?

00:05:23.767 --> 00:05:25.812
I heard they found him in the garage

00:05:25.847 --> 00:05:29.463
Locked inside his car
with the engine running.

00:05:30.327 --> 00:05:32.444
Do you know about what
time they found him?

00:05:32.479 --> 00:05:35.158
It just happened an hour or two ago.

00:05:35.193 --> 00:05:37.141
His poor family.

00:05:37.176 --> 00:05:40.950
I can't even imagine what
they're going through.

00:05:59.221 --> 00:06:00.829
Sam, we got here as fast as we could.

00:06:00.864 --> 00:06:02.955
Not fast enough.

00:06:03.585 --> 00:06:06.106
Which doesn't make any sense, man.

00:06:06.141 --> 00:06:08.157
Why would I even have these premonitions

00:06:08.192 --> 00:06:10.597
Unless there was a chance that
I can stop them from happening.

00:06:10.632 --> 00:06:12.298
I don't know.

00:06:17.637 --> 00:06:20.174
So, what do you think killed him?

00:06:20.376 --> 00:06:22.081
Maybe the guy killed himself.

00:06:22.116 --> 00:06:25.109
Maybe there's nothing
supernatural going on at all.

00:06:25.144 --> 00:06:27.824
I'm telling you. I watched it happen.

00:06:27.859 --> 00:06:30.504
He was murdered by something Dean.

00:06:30.539 --> 00:06:32.559
It trapped him in the garage.

00:06:32.594 --> 00:06:34.364
Like what? A spirit?
A poltergeist? What?

00:06:34.399 --> 00:06:35.856
I don't know what it was.

00:06:35.891 --> 00:06:38.085
I don't know why I'm
having these dreams.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.280
I don't know what the
hell is happening Dean.

00:06:40.555 --> 00:06:42.141
What?

00:06:42.176 --> 00:06:44.761
Nothing, man. I'm
just worried about you.

00:06:44.796 --> 00:06:46.867
Well, don't look at me like that.

00:06:46.902 --> 00:06:48.939
I'm not looking at you like anything.

00:06:49.163 --> 00:06:51.436
But I got to say. You look like crap.

00:06:51.471 --> 00:06:54.380
Nice, thanks. You welcome.

00:06:54.563 --> 00:06:57.355
Come on, let's just pick
this up in the morning.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.147
Check out the house,
we'll talk to the family.

00:07:00.607 --> 00:07:03.351
Dean, you saw them. They're devastated.

00:07:03.386 --> 00:07:06.095
They're not gonna want to talk to us.

00:07:07.517 --> 00:07:09.675
Yeah, you're right.

00:07:10.444 --> 00:07:13.005
But I think I know who they'll talk to.

00:07:14.079 --> 00:07:15.969
Who?

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:22.770
This has got to be a
whole new loaf for us.

00:07:27.258 --> 00:07:28.940
Good afternoon.

00:07:28.975 --> 00:07:31.560
I'm Father Simmons.
This is Father Freely.

00:07:31.595 --> 00:07:34.146
We're new junior priests
at Saint Augustine.

00:07:34.181 --> 00:07:35.989
May we come in?

00:07:37.137 --> 00:07:38.556
Thanks.

00:07:39.153 --> 00:07:41.143
We're very sorry for your loss.

00:07:43.046 --> 00:07:46.800
In difficult times like these when the
Lord's guidance is most needed. Look...

00:07:46.835 --> 00:07:49.349
You want to pitch your whole
Lord has a plan thing fine.

00:07:49.384 --> 00:07:51.800
Don't pitch it to me. My brother's dead.

00:07:51.835 --> 00:07:54.386
Roger, please.

00:07:55.869 --> 00:07:57.813
Excuse me.

00:08:00.364 --> 00:08:03.529
I'm sorry about my brother in law.

00:08:03.564 --> 00:08:06.695
He's just so upset about Jim's death.

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:08.375
Would you like some coffee?

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:10.083
That'll be great.

00:08:13.136 --> 00:08:16.138
It was wonderful of you to stop by.

00:08:16.173 --> 00:08:18.846
The support of the church
means so much right now.

00:08:18.881 --> 00:08:20.049
Of course.

00:08:20.084 --> 00:08:23.302
After all, we all are god's children.

00:08:30.789 --> 00:08:31.912
What?

00:08:31.947 --> 00:08:36.019
Just tone it down a little bit, Father.

00:08:41.013 --> 00:08:42.649
So, Ms. Miller.

00:08:42.684 --> 00:08:45.684
Did your husband have
a history of depression?

00:08:45.719 --> 00:08:47.501
Nothing like that.

00:08:47.536 --> 00:08:51.608
We... had our ups and
downs like everyone.

00:08:51.643 --> 00:08:54.054
But we were happy.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:58.234
I just don't understand

00:08:58.269 --> 00:09:01.740
How Jim could do something like that.

00:09:03.775 --> 00:09:07.424
I'm so sorry you had
to find him like that.

00:09:07.586 --> 00:09:09.814
Actually...

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:12.042
Our son, Max.

00:09:12.519 --> 00:09:15.523
He was the one who found him.

00:09:15.558 --> 00:09:18.335
Do you mind if maybe...
I go talk to him?

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:19.529
No.

00:09:19.564 --> 00:09:21.773
Oh, thank you Father.

00:09:33.765 --> 00:09:35.078
Max?

00:09:35.113 --> 00:09:37.015
Hey, I'm Sam.

00:09:40.734 --> 00:09:43.691
Ms. Miller, you have a lovely home.

00:09:44.181 --> 00:09:47.226
How long have you lived here?

00:09:47.261 --> 00:09:50.271
We moved in about five years ago.

00:09:51.115 --> 00:09:53.942
You know, the only problem
with these old houses

00:09:53.977 --> 00:09:57.163
I bet you have all kinds of headaches.

00:09:57.198 --> 00:09:59.164
Like what?

00:09:59.199 --> 00:10:01.095
Well...

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:03.653
Weird leaks.

00:10:03.688 --> 00:10:05.827
Electrical shortages.

00:10:05.862 --> 00:10:09.789
Odd sort of noises at
night. That kind of things.

00:10:11.136 --> 00:10:13.935
No, nothing like that.

00:10:14.105 --> 00:10:16.370
It's been perfect.

00:10:22.268 --> 00:10:23.657
May I use your restroom?

00:10:23.692 --> 00:10:26.310
Oh, sure. It's just up the stairs.

00:10:26.345 --> 00:10:27.829
Okay.

00:10:30.998 --> 00:10:33.515
So, what was your dad like?

00:10:34.593 --> 00:10:36.861
Just a normal dad.

00:10:36.896 --> 00:10:38.313
Yeah.

00:10:38.348 --> 00:10:41.573
You live at home now?

00:10:41.608 --> 00:10:43.186
Yeah.

00:10:43.221 --> 00:10:47.030
I'm trying to save up
for school but it's hard.

00:10:54.385 --> 00:10:57.795
So, when you found your dad?

00:10:58.730 --> 00:11:01.102
I woke up.

00:11:01.955 --> 00:11:04.782
I heard the engine running.

00:11:08.803 --> 00:11:11.744
I don't know why he did it.

00:11:15.088 --> 00:11:17.186
I know its ruff.

00:11:17.221 --> 00:11:19.250
Losing a parent.

00:11:19.285 --> 00:11:23.087
Especially when you don't
have all the answers.

00:12:18.159 --> 00:12:19.755
Anything?

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:21.395
Zip.

00:12:24.499 --> 00:12:27.083
Escanaba Motel No Vacancy

00:12:29.926 --> 00:12:32.238
So, what do you have? Well, nothing.

00:12:32.273 --> 00:12:35.101
Nothing bad has happened to the
Miller house since it was built.

00:12:35.136 --> 00:12:37.213
What about the land? No
graveyard, battlefields,

00:12:37.248 --> 00:12:42.286
Tribal lands or any other kind of
atrocity on or near the property.

00:12:43.017 --> 00:12:45.043
Hey, man. I told you. I
searched the house up and down.

00:12:45.078 --> 00:12:48.879
There were no cold spots,
no soul person, nada.

00:12:49.366 --> 00:12:51.353
And the family said
everything was normal.

00:12:51.388 --> 00:12:53.306
Well, if there was a
demon or poltergeist.

00:12:53.341 --> 00:12:55.139
You don't think somebody
would have notice something?

00:12:55.174 --> 00:12:58.256
I used the infrared thermo
scanner, man. There was nothing.

00:12:58.291 --> 00:13:00.743
So what? You think Jim
Miller killed himself?

00:13:00.778 --> 00:13:05.585
And my dream was some sort
of freakish coincidence?

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:07.154
I don't know.

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:10.635
I'm pretty sure there's nothing
supernatural about that house.

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:12.256
Yeah.

00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:13.842
Well...

00:13:14.517 --> 00:13:16.656
You know, maybe...

00:13:16.691 --> 00:13:18.970
Maybe there's nothing
to do with the house.

00:13:19.005 --> 00:13:21.217
Maybe it's just a...

00:13:21.252 --> 00:13:24.577
Gosh. Maybe it's connected to Jim.

00:13:24.612 --> 00:13:26.821
In some other way.

00:13:26.856 --> 00:13:29.031
What's wrong with you?

00:13:30.764 --> 00:13:32.140
My head!

00:13:32.175 --> 00:13:33.517
Sam?

00:13:35.145 --> 00:13:36.173
Hey!

00:13:36.399 --> 00:13:37.641
Hey!

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:40.021
What's going on? Talk to me.

00:15:20.104 --> 00:15:21.620
It's happening again!

00:15:21.655 --> 00:15:23.964
Something's gonna kill Roger Miller.

00:15:29.242 --> 00:15:31.022
Roger Miller?

00:15:31.679 --> 00:15:34.578
No, no, just the address please.

00:15:35.949 --> 00:15:37.810
Okay, thanks.

00:15:39.121 --> 00:15:43.265
450 West Grove. Apartment 1120.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:45.074
You okay?

00:15:45.323 --> 00:15:48.841
Yeah. If you're goon hurl. I'll
pull the car over, you know.

00:15:48.876 --> 00:15:51.288
I'm fine. Just drive.

00:15:51.323 --> 00:15:52.951
All right.

00:15:55.943 --> 00:15:57.469
Dean, I'm scared man.

00:15:57.504 --> 00:15:59.168
These nightmares weren't bad enough.

00:15:59.203 --> 00:16:00.833
Now I'm seeing things when I'm awake?

00:16:00.868 --> 00:16:02.258
And theses...

00:16:02.293 --> 00:16:08.497
Visions or whatever. They're
getting intense, painful.

00:16:08.532 --> 00:16:10.016
Come on man. You'll be all right.

00:16:10.051 --> 00:16:13.198
You'll be fine. What
is it about the Millers?

00:16:13.233 --> 00:16:18.356
Why am I connected to them?
Why am I watching them die?

00:16:18.574 --> 00:16:20.884
Why the hell is this happening
to me? I don't know Sam.

00:16:20.919 --> 00:16:22.901
But we'll figure it out, okay?

00:16:22.936 --> 00:16:25.969
We face the unexplainable every
single day. This is just another thing.

00:16:26.004 --> 00:16:28.512
No. It's never been us.

00:16:28.547 --> 00:16:31.137
It's never been in the family like this.

00:16:31.172 --> 00:16:34.814
Tell the truth. You can't tell
me this doesn't freak you out.

00:16:37.549 --> 00:16:39.833
This doesn't freak me out.

00:16:48.981 --> 00:16:50.295
Hey, Roger!

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:51.507
Hey, hold up a second.

00:16:51.542 --> 00:16:53.673
What are you guys,
missionaries? Leave me alone.

00:16:53.708 --> 00:16:55.227
Please!

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:02.105
Hey! Roger!

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:04.274
We're trying to help!
Please! Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:04.309 --> 00:17:06.026
Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:06.297 --> 00:17:08.062
I don't want your help.

00:17:08.097 --> 00:17:09.782
We're not priests. You've
got to listen to us!

00:17:09.817 --> 00:17:12.118
Roger, you're in danger!

00:17:13.738 --> 00:17:15.210
Come on, come on.

00:18:19.541 --> 00:18:20.747
Here.

00:18:21.317 --> 00:18:22.543
Start wiping down your finger prints.

00:18:22.578 --> 00:18:23.666
We don't want the cops
to know we were here.

00:18:23.701 --> 00:18:25.576
Go! Go! Come on!

00:18:29.878 --> 00:18:31.852
I'm gonna take a look inside.

00:18:37.855 --> 00:18:39.481
I'm telling you there
was nothing in there.

00:18:39.516 --> 00:18:41.818
There's no signs either.
Just like the Miller's house.

00:18:41.853 --> 00:18:44.873
I saw something in the
vision. Like a dark shape.

00:18:44.908 --> 00:18:46.077
Something was...

00:18:46.112 --> 00:18:47.831
Something was stalking Roger.

00:18:47.866 --> 00:18:50.665
Well, whatever it was I'm sure
it's not connected to their house.

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:52.862
No, it's connected to the family itself.

00:18:52.897 --> 00:18:55.335
So, what do you think?
Like a ventral spirit?

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:57.748
Oh, yeah. Few of them have been
known to ledge horn to families.

00:18:57.783 --> 00:18:59.356
They'll haunt them for years.

00:18:59.391 --> 00:19:02.142
Angier, Badges.

00:19:03.052 --> 00:19:04.522
Basically it was like a curse.

00:19:04.557 --> 00:19:07.158
Maybe Roger and Jim Miller got
involved in something heavy.

00:19:07.193 --> 00:19:10.337
Something curse worthy. And
now something's out for revenge.

00:19:10.372 --> 00:19:13.510
And they're making their family dying.

00:19:14.593 --> 00:19:17.345
Hey, you think Max is in danger?

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:20.062
Let's figure out before he is.

00:19:20.097 --> 00:19:23.324
Well... I know one thing I have
in common with these people.

00:19:23.359 --> 00:19:25.046
What's that?

00:19:25.081 --> 00:19:27.463
Well, their families are cursed.

00:19:27.498 --> 00:19:29.446
Our family's not cursed.

00:19:29.481 --> 00:19:32.832
We're just had our dark spots.

00:19:33.942 --> 00:19:35.497
Our dark spots are...

00:19:35.532 --> 00:19:37.656
Pretty dark.

00:19:37.691 --> 00:19:39.780
You're dark.

00:19:43.204 --> 00:19:47.054
My mom's resting. She's
pretty packed. Of course.

00:19:47.416 --> 00:19:50.633
All these people kept
coming with like casseroles.

00:19:50.668 --> 00:19:53.219
I finally had to tell
them all to go away.

00:19:53.254 --> 00:19:57.723
You know, cause nothing says
I'm sorry like a tuna casserole.

00:20:10.015 --> 00:20:12.532
How are you holding up?

00:20:12.714 --> 00:20:14.377
I'm okay.

00:20:14.412 --> 00:20:17.796
Your dad and your uncle were close?

00:20:17.831 --> 00:20:20.621
Yeah, I guess. They were brothers.

00:20:20.656 --> 00:20:23.377
I use to hang out when I was little.

00:20:23.412 --> 00:20:27.653
But not lately, much?
No, it's not that. It's...

00:20:27.688 --> 00:20:30.099
We used to be neighbors
when I was a kid.

00:20:30.134 --> 00:20:32.476
We lived across town
in this house and...

00:20:32.511 --> 00:20:37.252
Uncle Roger lived next door so
he was over all the time. Right.

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:42.526
So how was it in that
house when you were a kid?

00:20:42.561 --> 00:20:44.719
It was fine.

00:20:45.296 --> 00:20:46.641
Why?

00:20:46.676 --> 00:20:49.052
All good memories?

00:20:49.087 --> 00:20:51.851
You remember anything unusual?

00:20:51.886 --> 00:20:56.264
Something involving your
father and your uncle maybe?

00:20:57.451 --> 00:20:59.434
Why do you...?

00:20:59.608 --> 00:21:02.141
Why do you ask?

00:21:03.765 --> 00:21:06.212
It's just a question.

00:21:07.769 --> 00:21:12.061
No, there was nothing.
We were totally normal.

00:21:12.964 --> 00:21:15.933
Happy. Good.

00:21:16.803 --> 00:21:19.504
That's good.

00:21:20.145 --> 00:21:22.615
Well, you must be exhausted.

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:25.086
We should take off. Right.

00:21:26.158 --> 00:21:29.565
Thanks. Yeah.

00:21:33.509 --> 00:21:35.860
Nobody's family is
totally normal and happy.

00:21:35.895 --> 00:21:38.212
You see when he was
talking about his old house?

00:21:38.247 --> 00:21:40.331
Sounded scared.

00:21:40.366 --> 00:21:42.268
Max isn't telling us everything.

00:21:42.303 --> 00:21:44.135
See we go find the old neighborhood?

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:46.891
Find out what life it
was with the Millers.

00:21:51.333 --> 00:21:53.173
Have you lived in the
neighborhood very long?

00:21:53.208 --> 00:21:54.831
Yeah, almost twenty years now.

00:21:54.866 --> 00:21:56.049
It's nice and quiet.

00:21:56.084 --> 00:21:57.198
Why you looking to buy?

00:21:57.233 --> 00:21:59.248
No, no, actually we
were just wondering if...

00:21:59.283 --> 00:22:03.048
If you might recall a family that use to
live right across the street I believe.

00:22:03.083 --> 00:22:05.454
Yeah, the Millers. They
had a little boy named Max.

00:22:05.489 --> 00:22:07.177
Right.

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:09.003
Yeah, I remember.

00:22:09.038 --> 00:22:11.971
Their brother had the place next door.

00:22:12.248 --> 00:22:14.409
So, what's this about?

00:22:14.444 --> 00:22:16.545
That poor kid okay?

00:22:16.580 --> 00:22:18.646
What do you mean?

00:22:19.008 --> 00:22:22.118
Well, in my life. I've never
seen a child treated like that.

00:22:22.153 --> 00:22:23.452
I mean, I'd hear Mr. Miller

00:22:23.487 --> 00:22:26.872
Yelling and throwing things clear
across the street. He was a...

00:22:26.907 --> 00:22:28.616
Mean drunk.

00:22:28.651 --> 00:22:30.541
Used to beat the tire out of Max.

00:22:30.576 --> 00:22:34.329
Bruises. Broke his arm
two times that I know of.

00:22:34.364 --> 00:22:36.811
And this was going on regularly?

00:22:36.846 --> 00:22:38.607
Practically everyday.

00:22:38.642 --> 00:22:40.404
In fact that thug brother of his

00:22:40.439 --> 00:22:43.928
Was just as likely take a swing
at the boy. But the worst part...

00:22:43.963 --> 00:22:45.868
Was his step mother.

00:22:45.903 --> 00:22:48.085
She just...

00:22:48.120 --> 00:22:51.466
Stand there, checked out. Never
lifted a finger to protect him.

00:22:51.501 --> 00:22:54.082
I must have called the
police seven or eight times.

00:22:54.117 --> 00:22:56.664
Never did any good. Now,
you said 'step mother'.

00:22:56.699 --> 00:22:59.723
I think his real mom
died. Some sort of...

00:22:59.758 --> 00:23:02.647
Accident. Car accident I think.

00:23:02.682 --> 00:23:04.848
Are you okay there?

00:23:06.631 --> 00:23:08.832
Uh, yeah. Thanks for your time.

00:23:08.867 --> 00:23:11.034
Oh, yeah. Thank you. Let's go.

00:23:12.096 --> 00:23:13.803
Oh, god.

00:23:25.419 --> 00:23:28.045
I don't know what you mean by that.

00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:31.319
You know I didn't do
anything. That's right.

00:23:31.354 --> 00:23:34.857
You didn't do anything.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:39.219
You didn't stop them. Not once.

00:23:39.748 --> 00:23:41.763
How did you...?

00:23:44.498 --> 00:23:47.106
Max! Please!

00:23:59.085 --> 00:24:04.077
But every time you
stood there and watched.

00:24:04.112 --> 00:24:07.379
Pretending it wasn't happening.

00:24:07.414 --> 00:24:10.646
I'm sorry. No, you're not.

00:24:11.126 --> 00:24:14.180
You just don't want to die.

00:24:27.010 --> 00:24:28.880
Max is doing it.

00:24:28.915 --> 00:24:31.013
Everything I've been seeing.

00:24:31.048 --> 00:24:34.037
Are you sure about
this? Yeah, I saw him.

00:24:34.212 --> 00:24:35.630
How is he pulling it off?

00:24:35.665 --> 00:24:37.591
I don't know. Looks like telekinesis.

00:24:37.626 --> 00:24:39.482
So, he's Psychic? He's a spoon bender?

00:24:39.517 --> 00:24:42.146
I didn't even realize but
this whole time he was there.

00:24:42.181 --> 00:24:44.521
He was outside of the
garage when his dad died.

00:24:44.556 --> 00:24:46.862
He was in the apartment
when his uncle died.

00:24:46.897 --> 00:24:48.354
His visions this whole time.

00:24:48.389 --> 00:24:52.099
I wasn't connected to the
Millers. I was connecting to Max.

00:24:52.276 --> 00:24:55.054
The thing I don't know
is why man. I guess...

00:24:55.089 --> 00:24:56.902
Cause we are so alike?

00:24:56.937 --> 00:24:59.748
What are you talking about?
Dude's nothing like you.

00:24:59.783 --> 00:25:02.172
Oh, we both have psychic abilities.

00:25:02.207 --> 00:25:03.817
We're both... Both what?

00:25:03.852 --> 00:25:05.392
Sam, Max is a monster.

00:25:05.427 --> 00:25:07.386
He's already killed two people
now he's going for a third.

00:25:07.421 --> 00:25:10.107
With all he went through. The beatings.

00:25:10.142 --> 00:25:11.502
To want revenge on those people.

00:25:11.537 --> 00:25:14.163
I'm sorry man, I hate to
say it. It's not that insane.

00:25:14.198 --> 00:25:16.687
Yeah, but it doesn't justify
murdering your entire family.

00:25:16.722 --> 00:25:19.176
Dean... He's no different than
anything else we've hunted.

00:25:19.211 --> 00:25:21.124
All right, we've got to end it.

00:25:22.155 --> 00:25:24.271
We're not gonna kill Max.

00:25:24.306 --> 00:25:25.527
Then what?

00:25:25.562 --> 00:25:27.794
I hand him over to the cops
and say Lock him up, officer.

00:25:27.829 --> 00:25:30.227
He kills with his power
of his mind. Forget it.

00:25:30.262 --> 00:25:32.877
No way man. Sam! Do...

00:25:32.912 --> 00:25:34.673
He's a person.

00:25:34.708 --> 00:25:36.021
We can talk to him.

00:25:36.056 --> 00:25:39.773
Hey! Promise me you'll
follow my lead on this one.

00:25:40.663 --> 00:25:42.285
All right, fine.

00:25:42.320 --> 00:25:44.694
But I'm not letting
him hurt anyone else.

00:25:55.380 --> 00:25:59.338
You know I never did
anything. That's right.

00:25:59.373 --> 00:26:02.405
You didn't do anything.

00:26:02.682 --> 00:26:05.895
You didn't stop them. Not once.

00:26:06.991 --> 00:26:08.869
Fathers?

00:26:10.996 --> 00:26:14.332
What are you doing here? Oh...

00:26:14.367 --> 00:26:16.120
Sorry to interrupt.

00:26:16.155 --> 00:26:17.839
Max, could we uh...

00:26:17.874 --> 00:26:22.013
Could we talk to you
outside for just one second?

00:26:23.160 --> 00:26:25.287
About what?

00:26:25.322 --> 00:26:27.205
It's... It's private.

00:26:27.240 --> 00:26:30.016
Um... I wouldn't want to
bother your mother with it.

00:26:30.051 --> 00:26:33.026
We won't be long at
all though. I promise.

00:26:39.087 --> 00:26:40.528
Okay.

00:26:40.563 --> 00:26:41.969
Great.

00:27:08.117 --> 00:27:10.146
You're not priests!

00:27:16.245 --> 00:27:17.555
Max! What's happening?

00:27:17.590 --> 00:27:19.896
Shut up! What are you doing?

00:27:22.553 --> 00:27:24.843
I said shut up! Max, calm down.

00:27:24.878 --> 00:27:26.786
Who are you? We just
want to talk to you.

00:27:26.821 --> 00:27:28.695
Yeah, right. That's
why you brought this.

00:27:28.730 --> 00:27:30.389
That was a mistake, all right?

00:27:30.424 --> 00:27:32.651
So was lying about who we
were. But no more lying Max.

00:27:32.686 --> 00:27:34.480
Okay? Just please.

00:27:34.515 --> 00:27:37.762
Just hear me out. About what?

00:27:38.203 --> 00:27:40.847
I saw you do it.

00:27:40.882 --> 00:27:44.993
I saw you kill your dad and
your uncle before it happened.

00:27:45.028 --> 00:27:48.658
What? I'm having visions about you.

00:27:48.693 --> 00:27:50.550
You're crazy.

00:27:50.585 --> 00:27:52.842
So, you weren't gonna launch
a knife at your step mom?

00:27:52.877 --> 00:27:54.171
Right here?

00:27:54.206 --> 00:27:56.719
Isn't that hard to believe?
Max, look what you can do?

00:27:56.754 --> 00:27:59.630
Max, I was drawn here, all right?

00:28:00.207 --> 00:28:03.071
I think I'm here to help you.

00:28:05.943 --> 00:28:08.523
No one can help me.

00:28:08.558 --> 00:28:09.883
Let me try.

00:28:09.918 --> 00:28:11.330
We'll just talk.

00:28:11.365 --> 00:28:12.674
Me and you.

00:28:12.709 --> 00:28:16.938
We'll get Dean and Alice
out of here. No, no way.

00:28:17.651 --> 00:28:19.765
Nobody leaves this house!

00:28:19.800 --> 00:28:22.251
And nobody has to, all
right? They'll just...

00:28:22.286 --> 00:28:23.528
They'll just go upstairs.

00:28:23.563 --> 00:28:25.313
Sam, I'm not leaving you alone with him.

00:28:25.348 --> 00:28:26.961
Yes, you are.

00:28:26.996 --> 00:28:28.540
Look, Max...

00:28:28.575 --> 00:28:30.818
You're in charge here. All
right? We all know that.

00:28:30.853 --> 00:28:33.061
No one's gonna do anything
that you don't want to do.

00:28:33.096 --> 00:28:36.625
But I'm talking five
minutes here man. Sam...

00:28:39.242 --> 00:28:41.475
Five minutes?

00:28:42.553 --> 00:28:43.961
Go.

00:28:56.780 --> 00:28:58.147
Come on.

00:29:02.776 --> 00:29:04.199
Look.

00:29:04.234 --> 00:29:06.800
I can't begin to understand
what you went through.

00:29:06.835 --> 00:29:09.442
That's right, you can't. Max...

00:29:09.477 --> 00:29:11.960
This has to stop. It will.

00:29:11.995 --> 00:29:14.443
After my step mother... No.

00:29:14.478 --> 00:29:16.428
You need to let her go.

00:29:16.463 --> 00:29:18.235
Why?

00:29:19.189 --> 00:29:21.143
Did she beat you?

00:29:21.178 --> 00:29:22.493
No.

00:29:22.528 --> 00:29:27.126
But she never tried to save
me. She's part of it too.

00:29:28.356 --> 00:29:30.087
Look what they did to you.

00:29:30.122 --> 00:29:34.016
Look what they all
did to you growing up.

00:29:34.051 --> 00:29:37.911
They deserve to be punished. Growing up?

00:29:37.946 --> 00:29:40.806
Try last week.

00:29:46.295 --> 00:29:48.312
My dad still hits me.

00:29:48.347 --> 00:29:51.847
Just in places people wouldn't see it.

00:29:52.848 --> 00:29:55.994
Old habits die hard I guess.

00:29:59.720 --> 00:30:01.654
I'm sorry.

00:30:07.118 --> 00:30:11.017
When I first found out
I could move things.

00:30:11.052 --> 00:30:13.356
It was a gift.

00:30:13.840 --> 00:30:17.560
My whole life I was helpless.

00:30:17.595 --> 00:30:20.163
But now I have this.

00:30:21.030 --> 00:30:23.333
So, last week...

00:30:23.368 --> 00:30:25.602
Dad gets drunk.

00:30:25.637 --> 00:30:28.085
First time in a long time.

00:30:28.120 --> 00:30:30.498
And he beats me to hell.

00:30:30.533 --> 00:30:33.274
It's the first time in a long time.

00:30:33.510 --> 00:30:36.225
And I do what I had to do.

00:30:36.260 --> 00:30:39.016
Why didn't you just leave?

00:30:39.051 --> 00:30:41.772
It isn't about getting away.

00:30:42.744 --> 00:30:46.868
Just knowing that they'd
still be out there.

00:30:47.151 --> 00:30:52.248
It was about not being afraid.

00:30:53.953 --> 00:30:56.736
When my dad used to look at me.

00:30:56.771 --> 00:30:59.484
There was hate in his eyes.

00:30:59.519 --> 00:31:03.061
Do you know what that feels like?

00:31:05.218 --> 00:31:06.481
No.

00:31:06.516 --> 00:31:09.609
He blamed me for everything.

00:31:09.644 --> 00:31:12.703
For his job. For his life.

00:31:12.738 --> 00:31:15.529
For my mom's death.

00:31:15.564 --> 00:31:18.876
Why did he blame you
for your mom's death?

00:31:21.498 --> 00:31:24.215
Because she died in my nursery.

00:31:24.250 --> 00:31:27.565
While I was asleep in my crib.

00:31:27.600 --> 00:31:30.881
As if that makes it my fault.

00:31:31.097 --> 00:31:33.145
She died in your nursery?

00:31:33.180 --> 00:31:34.389
Yeah.

00:31:34.424 --> 00:31:37.502
There was a fire and he get drunk

00:31:37.537 --> 00:31:41.602
And blab along like she
died in some insane way.

00:31:41.637 --> 00:31:44.029
He said that she burned up.

00:31:44.064 --> 00:31:46.895
Pinned to the ceiling.

00:31:52.017 --> 00:31:54.139
Listen to me Max.

00:31:54.609 --> 00:31:56.265
What your dad said.

00:31:56.300 --> 00:31:59.004
About what happened to your mom.

00:31:59.951 --> 00:32:02.203
It's real.

00:32:03.357 --> 00:32:05.053
What?

00:32:05.088 --> 00:32:07.105
It happened to my mom too.

00:32:07.140 --> 00:32:09.061
Exactly the same.

00:32:09.096 --> 00:32:10.947
My nursery, my crib.

00:32:10.982 --> 00:32:13.753
My dad saw her in the ceiling.

00:32:14.294 --> 00:32:17.674
Your dad must have been
as drunk as mine. No.

00:32:17.709 --> 00:32:19.571
No, it's the same thing, Max.

00:32:19.606 --> 00:32:21.831
The same thing killed our mothers.

00:32:21.866 --> 00:32:24.176
That's impossible.

00:32:24.525 --> 00:32:28.117
This must be why I've been
having visions during the day.

00:32:28.291 --> 00:32:30.674
Why they're getting more intense.

00:32:30.866 --> 00:32:34.308
Cause you and I must be
connected in some way.

00:32:34.490 --> 00:32:37.346
Your abilities started six,
seven months ago, right?

00:32:37.381 --> 00:32:39.193
Out of the blue?

00:32:39.469 --> 00:32:40.544
How'd you know that?

00:32:40.579 --> 00:32:42.603
Because that's when my
abilities started Max.

00:32:42.638 --> 00:32:45.218
I mean, yours seem to be much
further along but still this...

00:32:45.253 --> 00:32:47.444
This means something. Right?

00:32:47.479 --> 00:32:52.404
I mean, for some reason.
You and I were chosen.

00:32:54.119 --> 00:32:56.290
For what?

00:32:57.154 --> 00:32:59.162
I don't know.

00:32:59.909 --> 00:33:02.114
But Dean and I... My brother and I...

00:33:02.149 --> 00:33:04.320
We're hunting for your mom's killer.

00:33:04.355 --> 00:33:06.003
We can find answers.

00:33:06.038 --> 00:33:08.614
Answers that can answer us both.

00:33:08.649 --> 00:33:11.191
But you got to let us go Max.

00:33:11.533 --> 00:33:14.826
You got to let your step mother go.

00:33:27.693 --> 00:33:29.637
No.

00:33:30.140 --> 00:33:32.987
What they did to me.

00:33:33.022 --> 00:33:35.799
I still have nightmares.

00:33:35.834 --> 00:33:38.563
I'm still scared all the time. Like...

00:33:38.598 --> 00:33:41.042
I'm waiting for that next beating.

00:33:41.077 --> 00:33:45.076
I'm just tired of being scared.
If I do this, it'll be all over.

00:33:45.111 --> 00:33:46.689
No, don't you get it?

00:33:46.724 --> 00:33:47.807
It won't.

00:33:47.842 --> 00:33:49.614
The nightmares won't end Max.

00:33:49.649 --> 00:33:51.459
Not like this.

00:33:51.494 --> 00:33:53.270
There's just...

00:33:53.431 --> 00:33:55.400
More pain.

00:33:55.643 --> 00:33:58.276
And it makes you as bad as them.

00:33:59.075 --> 00:34:01.155
Max...

00:34:01.742 --> 00:34:05.326
You don't have to go
this all by yourself.

00:34:10.241 --> 00:34:12.409
I'm sorry.

00:34:13.119 --> 00:34:14.564
No!

00:34:15.346 --> 00:34:16.946
Max!

00:34:18.777 --> 00:34:20.222
No!

00:34:20.257 --> 00:34:21.667
Max!

00:34:46.511 --> 00:34:47.873
Max!

00:34:50.088 --> 00:34:51.679
Son of a...

00:34:53.403 --> 00:34:54.775
Max.

00:34:55.380 --> 00:34:56.949
Max.

00:35:00.208 --> 00:35:01.743
No.

00:35:10.472 --> 00:35:12.067
Max.

00:35:13.587 --> 00:35:15.724
Stay back.

00:35:16.084 --> 00:35:17.918
It's not about you.

00:35:17.953 --> 00:35:21.012
If you want to kill. You got
to go through with me first.

00:35:22.349 --> 00:35:23.996
Okay.

00:35:42.394 --> 00:35:43.683
No!

00:35:44.415 --> 00:35:45.998
No!

00:35:57.655 --> 00:35:59.522
Max...

00:36:00.421 --> 00:36:02.132
No.

00:36:02.518 --> 00:36:04.634
Stay back.

00:36:04.832 --> 00:36:06.534
It's not about you.

00:36:06.569 --> 00:36:10.064
If you want to kill. You got
to go through with me first.

00:36:10.873 --> 00:36:12.741
Okay.

00:36:14.442 --> 00:36:16.973
No, don't! Don't!

00:36:17.008 --> 00:36:19.505
Please! Please Max!

00:36:20.607 --> 00:36:22.137
Max...

00:36:22.172 --> 00:36:24.551
We can help you.

00:36:24.764 --> 00:36:27.715
But this... What you're doing...

00:36:27.936 --> 00:36:30.052
It's not the solution.

00:36:30.087 --> 00:36:33.400
It's not gonna fix anything.

00:36:43.477 --> 00:36:46.009
You're right.

00:36:48.667 --> 00:36:50.192
No!

00:37:00.597 --> 00:37:02.819
Max attacked me.

00:37:02.854 --> 00:37:05.627
He threatened me with a gun.

00:37:06.330 --> 00:37:08.261
And these two?

00:37:10.214 --> 00:37:12.272
They're...

00:37:12.307 --> 00:37:14.731
Family friends.

00:37:15.779 --> 00:37:20.380
I called them as soon as
Max arrived. I was scared.

00:37:20.570 --> 00:37:23.088
They tried to stop him.

00:37:23.123 --> 00:37:25.607
They fought for the gun.

00:37:25.807 --> 00:37:28.669
Where did Max hid the gun?

00:37:30.511 --> 00:37:33.863
I don't know. He...

00:37:33.898 --> 00:37:37.215
Showed up and he...

00:37:40.653 --> 00:37:42.955
It's all right, Mrs. Miller.

00:37:44.405 --> 00:37:47.698
I lost everyone.

00:37:48.803 --> 00:37:50.403
Okay.

00:37:50.739 --> 00:37:52.826
We'll give you a call if we
have any further questions.

00:37:52.861 --> 00:37:54.624
Thanks officer.

00:37:55.076 --> 00:37:56.499
Come on.

00:38:09.167 --> 00:38:11.906
Freggis said something else.

00:38:11.941 --> 00:38:14.578
Got him through it
somehow. Don't do that.

00:38:14.613 --> 00:38:16.811
Do what? Told you yourself.

00:38:16.846 --> 00:38:19.689
It wouldn't matter what you
said. Max was too far gone.

00:38:19.724 --> 00:38:22.532
When I think about how he
looked at me man right before...

00:38:22.726 --> 00:38:24.064
I should have done something.

00:38:24.099 --> 00:38:26.283
Come on, man. You risked your life.

00:38:26.318 --> 00:38:29.725
I mean, yeah. If we gotten
there twenty years earlier...

00:38:31.626 --> 00:38:33.380
Well, I'll tell you one thing.

00:38:33.415 --> 00:38:35.551
We're lucky we had dad.

00:38:38.171 --> 00:38:41.728
I never thought you say that.

00:38:41.931 --> 00:38:43.205
Well...

00:38:43.240 --> 00:38:45.862
He could have gone away more after mom.

00:38:45.897 --> 00:38:51.393
A little more tequila a
little less demon hunting.

00:38:51.428 --> 00:38:54.860
Then we would have Max's childhood.

00:38:55.945 --> 00:38:58.355
All things considered.

00:38:58.390 --> 00:39:00.766
We turned out okay.

00:39:00.801 --> 00:39:03.116
Thanks to him.

00:39:06.817 --> 00:39:09.016
All things considered.

00:39:18.155 --> 00:39:19.411
Dean, I've been thinking.

00:39:19.446 --> 00:39:20.632
That's never a good thing.

00:39:20.667 --> 00:39:23.584
I'm serious. I've been thinking...

00:39:23.619 --> 00:39:27.328
Why would this demon or
whatever it is. Why would it...

00:39:27.363 --> 00:39:29.786
Kill mom and Jessica and Max's mother?

00:39:29.821 --> 00:39:31.409
You know, what does it want?

00:39:31.444 --> 00:39:33.643
No idea. Well, you think maybe...

00:39:33.678 --> 00:39:36.615
It was after us? After...

00:39:36.650 --> 00:39:39.457
Max and me? Why would you think that?

00:39:39.690 --> 00:39:40.964
I mean...

00:39:40.999 --> 00:39:42.962
Either telekinesis are premonitions.

00:39:42.997 --> 00:39:44.891
We both had abilities, you know.

00:39:44.926 --> 00:39:47.063
Maybe it was after us for some reason.

00:39:47.098 --> 00:39:50.212
Sam, if it wanted you. It
would have just taken you.

00:39:50.247 --> 00:39:51.398
Okay?

00:39:51.433 --> 00:39:53.010
This is not your fault.

00:39:53.045 --> 00:39:54.829
It is not about you.

00:39:54.864 --> 00:39:56.613
Then what is it about?

00:39:56.812 --> 00:39:59.289
It's about that damn thing
that did this to our family.

00:39:59.324 --> 00:40:02.072
That thing that we're gonna
find that thing we're gonna kill.

00:40:02.107 --> 00:40:04.218
And that's all.

00:40:05.497 --> 00:40:07.920
Actually, there's a...

00:40:07.955 --> 00:40:10.343
Something else too.

00:40:10.969 --> 00:40:12.346
Oh, geez what?

00:40:12.381 --> 00:40:15.584
When Max locked me in that closet.

00:40:15.619 --> 00:40:18.787
That big cabinet against the door.

00:40:19.139 --> 00:40:21.138
I moved it.

00:40:22.157 --> 00:40:25.016
Yeah, you're a little more up the body
strength than I gave you credit for.

00:40:25.051 --> 00:40:28.028
No man. I moved it. Like...

00:40:28.063 --> 00:40:30.164
Max.

00:40:32.908 --> 00:40:34.717
Oh.

00:40:36.636 --> 00:40:38.590
Right.

00:40:38.625 --> 00:40:40.544
Yeah.

00:40:47.233 --> 00:40:49.401
Bend this.

00:40:49.640 --> 00:40:51.312
I can't turn it on and off Dean.

00:40:51.347 --> 00:40:52.775
Then how'd you do it? I don't know.

00:40:52.810 --> 00:40:54.939
I can't control it. I just...

00:40:54.974 --> 00:40:58.511
I saw you die and it just came
out of me like a... Like a punch.

00:40:58.546 --> 00:40:59.827
You know, like a...

00:40:59.862 --> 00:41:02.633
Like a freak adrenaline thing.

00:41:06.276 --> 00:41:08.778
Well, I'm sure it won't happen again.

00:41:10.534 --> 00:41:12.266
Yeah, maybe.

00:41:12.301 --> 00:41:13.430
Aren't you worried man?

00:41:13.465 --> 00:41:16.143
Aren't you worried that I can
turn into Max or something?

00:41:16.178 --> 00:41:18.889
Nope. No way.

00:41:19.078 --> 00:41:20.273
You know why?

00:41:20.308 --> 00:41:21.959
No, why?

00:41:21.994 --> 00:41:24.230
Cause you got one advantage
that Max didn't have.

00:41:24.265 --> 00:41:25.983
Dad?

00:41:26.154 --> 00:41:28.392
Because dad's not here, Dean.

00:41:28.427 --> 00:41:30.070
No.

00:41:30.666 --> 00:41:32.748
Me.

00:41:33.897 --> 00:41:35.591
As long as I'm around...

00:41:35.626 --> 00:41:38.384
Nothing bad is gonna happen to you.

00:41:39.956 --> 00:41:41.653
Now then.

00:41:41.688 --> 00:41:44.526
I know what we need to
do with your premonitions.

00:41:44.561 --> 00:41:46.549
I know where we've got to go.

00:41:46.584 --> 00:41:48.599
Where?

00:41:48.830 --> 00:41:50.924
Vegas.

00:41:54.769 --> 00:41:57.088
What? Come on man.

00:41:57.285 --> 00:42:00.411
Craps table. We'd clean up.



00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
